 in a 16-week trial (full citation: [Author et al., JAMA Psychiatry, 2022, doi: 10.1001/xxx — access the primary source for full methodology and results]). Member organizations are self-selected and findings may not represent the broader DTx developer community.\"\n\n[Source M — Bundesministerium für Gesundheit, \"DiGA Verzeichnis,\" July 2024]\nExcerpt: \"As of 1 July 2024, 52 digital health applications have received DiGA listing (permanent or provisional). DiGA listings include both permanently approved applications meeting full evidence standards and provisionally approved applications with evidence generation still in progress.\"\n\n---\nProduce: (1) revised brief with inline source pointers, (2) unsupported-claims log."